# Keep every byte of this repository the way it was written.
#
# Two corpus cases are *about* bytes rather than about text:
#
#   crlf_check      a source file whose line endings are CR LF, not LF
#   bom_check       a source file whose first three bytes are EF BB BF
#
# Git's line-ending normalisation would rewrite those files in the working tree on
# checkout, which would silently change what those cases test — and the same
# normalisation turns a diff of the corpus into noise, in a project whose whole
# evidence culture is "show the measurement".
#
# `-text` on everything disables the conversion for every file, so what is
# committed is what was written, byte for byte.  No file here needs the opposite
# treatment: the Vela sources, the goldens, the emitted C that is tracked (the
# bootstrap `selfhost/build/vm.c`), and the PowerShell tools all work as they are.
* -text
